WEBVTT

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.570
I am Inudou Shirosuke, 
Warden of Abashiri Prison.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:08.820
Nice to meet you.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:11.240
Inudou...

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.640
Um... who is this?

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.580
Sugimoto, my guard.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:24.250
Five years ago, a brutal criminal 
named Ienaga bit off his face.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:28.440
He may look like this, but he's
 very good at his job.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.660
Inudou...

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:33.340
Very sorry to hear that.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.610
I dunno how that actually worked.

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.090
I was told Shiraishi Yoshitake is here.

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.020
I want him sent back to Abashiri.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:48.780
Shiraishi? There's no 
man here with that name.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.440
<i>Where did he find out? Who told him?</i>

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.510
I don't like being told lies to to my face!

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.770
Inu... dou...

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:06.010
Not only did you illegally transport 
prisoners from Abashiri during my absence,

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.080
you allowed all of them to escape.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:15.770
I'm trying to clean up the 
mess that you, the 7th, made,

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.130
Regiment Commander!

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.030
Contact Lt. Tsurumi in Otaru.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:25.940
Now.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.750
<b>Otaru</b>

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.770
A man calling himself 
Inudou Shirosuke? In Asahikawa?

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.050
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:16.480
<b>Episode Seventeen
Inside the Belly</b>

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:14.960
All this money...

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:17.730
What are you thinking?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.000
Are you telling me you'll buy 
Shiraishi Yoshitake with this money?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.090
No. These bills are fake.

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:29.480
This is the plate used to make them.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.190
Confiscated from a genius 
counterfeiter we arrested.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.280
Are you aware of the Continental dollar
 during the American Revolution,

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.920
or Napoleon's counterfeit gulden?

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.200
Spreading counterfeit 
currency in a time of war

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.910
to cause economic chaos is an 
extremely effective measure.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:51.780
He would be able to make an accurate 
copy of any nation's currency.

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:57.380
I think he'd be quite a valuable asset 
to the Japanese Army in the future.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:01.450
Are you interested?

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:07.570
<i>I thought he was just a 
washed-up marriage fraudster.</i>

00:04:07.570 --> 00:04:10.920
<i>This explains why Hijikata 
kept him as a secret weapon.</i>

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.120
<i>Suzukawa Kiyohiro is no ordinary con artist!</i>

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.720
<i>One more push and the 
Lt. Colonel will give in!</i>

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.530
I'll offer you a trade.
Shiraishi for the counterfeiter.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.970
Lt. Colonel Yodogawa...

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:33.540
After the Russo-Japanese War, every other
 lieutenant colonel made full colonel.

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:38.440
But you haven't.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.290
Don't you think you're 
being treated unfairly?

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:48.050
This will be your path to promotion.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.040
<b>Otaru Telephone Exchange</b>

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:54.590
Hello, is this a local or long-distance call?

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.980
<i>Long-distance! Connect me to the 7th Division
 in Asahikawa, Regiment 27's Command HQ!</i>

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:04.070
It's Tsurumi! Don't go along with 
Lt. Colonel Yodogawa's decision!

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:06.950
Don't let anybody see Shiraishi!

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:10.420
If Inudou Shirosuke were to take 
a single step out of Abashiri,

00:05:10.420 --> 00:05:14.960
my men there would tell me!

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.970
You're too close to the 
receiver, Lt. Tsurumi!

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:16.960
Send Second Lt. Koito there, now!

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.080
That's...

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.070
That's not good.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:24.930
That's one of Lt. Tsurumi's 
favorite Satsuma messengers.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.190
What is this?

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.250
What's going on?

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.850
One of my men is out front 
with the counterfeiter.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.850
Let's do the exchange with Shiraishi outside.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:47.610
After the incident at Abashiri, 
I trust you far less.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.620
<i>I see...</i>

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.150
<i>They look a lot alike,</i>

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.620
<i>but this is a fake Inudou.</i>

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.880
<i>And from the shape of his clothes,</i>

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.030
<i>the weirdo is Sugimoto.</i>

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:01.630
<i>They came to get me back?</i>

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.300
What is it, Second Lt. Koito?

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:16.650
Lt. Tsurumi told you not to let anybody make 
contact with Shiraishi until he arrives.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.690
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.420
<i>He works for Tsurumi?</i>

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:26.600
Are you forced to obey the 
lieutenant's orders, Lt. Colonel Yodogawa?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.610
Leave. Nobody called for you.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.280
Inudou-sama...

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.990
Chinchin nukinammoshita naa.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:37.540
Chinchin...?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:45.250
I've heard that Inudou-sama spent 
a great deal of time with prisoners

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:48.430
from Satsuma during his time as warden 
of Kabato Prison in Tsukigata,

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:52.390
and is thus able to speak 
the Satsuma dialect well.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.750
Koito, what are you doing?

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:58.560
Sakki, oiga nanchuutaka, kotaetemikkunyanse.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.820
Yo ga heruto hiekkumonde na.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.320
Chinchin nukinammoshita naa.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.320
It's gotten warmer lately.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.470
Yo ga heruto hiekkumonde na.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.470
It's cold at night, though.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.040
<i>That's why he's a genius, I guess.</i>

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:20.140
<i>He mastered that in such a short time.</i>

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.750
Asa wa teabui ga irimosuna

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.750
You need a brazier in the morning.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.170
Waga bakkaishii choddo.

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.170
I never let anyone else use mine.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.130
Tsuggyage kuuta kogga aimosuka.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.130
Have you ever had fried satsuma-age?

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.430
Sake no shioke ni gattsui jaddo.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.430
They're the perfect snack when you're drinking.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:37.080
<i>I have no idea what they're saying.</i>

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:39.390
<i>Are they really both Japanese?</i>

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:42.230
Jujo nanongoro jaddokimmoshita.

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:42.230
I heard you liked to drink.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.250
Imagowa yoonarimoshita.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.250
Not as much as I used to.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:57.010
Lt. Tsurumi's information told me that 
Inudou Shirosuke couldn't drink at all.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.580
Bastards...

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.610
I should've just thrown him 
into the goddamn river!

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.420
Wait!

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:09.430
Don't kill Shiraishi!

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:11.170
Lt. Tsurumi will get mad at you!

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.010
And by you, I mean me!

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:14.950
Sugimoto!

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:18.100
I am Immortal Sugimoto!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:21.610
After them!

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:22.350
Yes, sir!

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:24.810
They have allies outside?

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:27.940
Ow...

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.340
This way, Shiraishi!

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.280
Kiroranke and the others have horses waiting!

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:34.240
Sugimoto, are you okay?

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:36.020
Run, Shiraishi!

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.570
Don't let them get away!

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:42.880
Sugimoto, you can't get out this way!

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.560
Run to the south! That way!

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:49.670
Those gunshots made the 
bees leave their nests.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.500
Sugimoto was shot!

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.050
He's immortal, right?

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:57.970
Run or die.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:02.440
That's crazy! Sugimoto's hurt,
 he can't keep running!

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.210
If I stop running...

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:09.570
Shiraishi, you take Asirpa-san 
to Abashiri Prison.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.990
What the hell is that?

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:26.050
A prototype for a hot air balloon unit.

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:28.790
That's it! Let's steal it!

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:33.430
Everyone, get back!

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:34.460
Further back!

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.430
Give it to me!

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.390
I said hurry it up!

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:40.350
Get back, or we'll shoot!

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:44.010
You can't! You might ignite the hydrogen!

00:09:44.010 --> 00:09:44.980
Capture them!

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.110
Let go, damn it!

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:57.030
That's my sword!

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:14.550
Second Lt. Koito!

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.590
What the hell is that?

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.060
Sugimoto's group is on it!

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:24.390
So those gunshots were from them!

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:26.360
They're using that to escape.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:36.580
Give me a bayonet. I'll handle this.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:39.400
He uses Jigen style,
traditional Satsuma swordsmanship.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:42.870
You can't fight him with two bullets in you.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.890
Ogata Hyakunosuke!

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.500
You bastard!

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:50.290
Yokumo Tsurumi Chuuidon 
wo damakesee uragitta na!

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:50.290
You'll pay for betraying Lt. Tsurumi!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.330
Maekara wai no kotsu wa wazzeesukankatta!

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:52.330
I never liked you to begin with!

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.510
Oiga kotsu bonbon 
chinamekusassee shirantokoide

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.510
I know you thought I was just some rich brat,

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:56.340
ware kobbobbakai iuchotta to wa shichotta!

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:56.340
and kept insulting me behind my back!

00:10:56.380 --> 00:11:01.660
As usual, I have no idea what 
you're saying, Second Lt. Koito.

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:05.100
When you get upset, you start 
talking quickly in Satsuma dialect.

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:08.060
Waitacha zuruttatakikiddo!

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:08.060
I'll kill you all!!

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:09.520
Don't block it!

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.030
Shiraishi!

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:29.200
Shiraishi!

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:36.670
Oboecchoreyo! Waitacha zurut Tsurumi 
Chuuidon ni gararuddena!

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:36.670
Lt. Tsurumi is gonna get mad at all of you!!

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:40.120
Bye-bye, Koito-chan!

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:42.720
Shiraishi, you're about 
to slam into the trees!

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.870
Ow!

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:50.180
<i>Ow</i>!

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.190
Asirpa-san!

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:11.140
Tsurumi Chuuidon ni garareru...

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:11.140
Lt. Tsurumi is gonna be mad at me...

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.960
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.730
One of the bullets passed 
through your shoulder,

00:12:22.730 --> 00:12:25.190
but the other is still in your left breast.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.680
We need to get it out later.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:31.080
You took a risk like that to get me back?

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:35.650
I'm the Escape King! 
I could've gotten away myself.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:38.300
Everyone was going to give up on you.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:41.740
It was Sugimoto who said we had to save you.

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.740
Really?

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.530
You'll help us when we get 
to Abashiri. I know it.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:52.050
I believed in you. 
That's why I decided to save you.

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:57.040
But I remembered something, Shiraishi.

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:02.590
That strange old man we met at 
the herring fishery longhouse...

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:08.850
You were working with Hijikata, weren't you?

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:16.590
Wait, Shiraishi!

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.520
Don't run away! Look at this!

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:22.780
That's...

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:28.110
The copy of Henmi Kazuo's tattoos 
that you gave to Ushiyama in Sapporo.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:31.020
Hijikata Toshizou showed it to me.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.740
I took a careful look...

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:36.970
And it was a fake.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:42.960
Shiraishi never betrayed us.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:46.050
Yes, that's right!

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.910
I told you that I'd bet on you!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.440
Hey... It's acting weird.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:05.670
Stop it.

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:12.950
That's dangerous!

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.160
Pawci casi.

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:18.320
It means "village where 
the Pawci-Kamuy live."

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:20.580
It's said to be the fortress 
of the Pawci-Kamuy.

00:14:21.010 --> 00:14:25.090
The Pawci are sex demons. Not very good gods.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:29.050
Anyone they possess will strip off 
their clothes and start dancing.

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.130
That's ridiculous.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.270
The Ainu have big imaginations, huh?

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:43.090
We're about forty kilometers away 
from the 7th Division's barracks.

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:46.440
I saw soldiers on horses 
following us from the air.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:50.450
That thing's not exactly hard to spot. 
They'll know about where we are.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:52.780
If we don't hurry, they'll catch up to you.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.000
We need to treat Sugimoto.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:59.370
I found some retannoya, or alpine yarrow.

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:01.210
Put its crushed leaves on the wound,

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.790
and they can stop the bleeding.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:06.340
Second Lt. Koito shot me
with a Type 26 revolver.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:08.730
Once, somebody shot that gun at a pig's nose,

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:09.930
and the bullet bounced right off.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:11.520
It's incredibly weak.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:14.300
You can't kill me with something like that.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.350
Suzukawa was weaker than 
a pig's nose, though.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.690
Suzukawa was killed?

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.400
They found us!

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.870
Hurry! We need to cross the 
Daisetsuzan to flee.

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:44.050
Seriously? Those mountains?

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:49.800
<b>Daisetsuzan</b>

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.180
Oh, no! The weather's suddenly gotten bad!

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:57.720
The wind is so cold.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.770
The wind's just going to get stronger, 
and it will start raining, too!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.490
This is impossible! Let's head back!

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:04.650
Don't be stupid! They're following us!

00:16:04.650 --> 00:16:06.740
Do we dig a hole in the snow and hide there?

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:09.610
No! There's not enough snow left to do it!

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:15.010
Shiraishi's acting strange!

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:17.000
Look for a place to hide from the wind!

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.040
Or you'll die from hypothermia!

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:21.410
Yuk!

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.390
Sugimoto, shoot the bucks! 
We need three of the big ones!

00:16:25.390 --> 00:16:26.710
We shoot the deer?

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:31.690
Two at the same time?

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.060
Hurry and skin them!

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.420
It doesn't have to be a perfect job!

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:38.590
We'll hide in the deer's bodies?

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.330
Inside the deer's corpses?

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.710
A Pawci Kamuy got him!

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:50.030
He's gone crazy!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.160
Shiraishi!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:53.490
Sugimoto, you can't run with that wound!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:55.780
You and Ogata need to skin the deer!

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.360
Shiraishi?

00:17:04.390 --> 00:17:05.870
Asirpa-san is still...

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:09.500
Hey, Sugimoto!

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:24.350
Asirpa-san! Asirpa-san!

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:29.800
Where are you, Asirpa-san?

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.800
Sugimoto!

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:35.410
Sugimoto!

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:42.240
I lost Shiraishi.

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:43.830
He came back.

00:17:44.690 --> 00:17:45.920
Great.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.190
Asirpa-san, are you okay? You look pale.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.260
I'm fine.

00:17:50.260 --> 00:17:51.560
What about you?

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:52.570
Let's head back.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:01.940
Sugimoto!

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:13.780
Why didn't you shoot?

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:18.660
This thing is me!

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:44.360
Does your wound bother you, Sugimoto?

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:48.920
I'm fine. It'll be better 
by tomorrow morning.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:53.920
Did Suzukawa suffer?

00:18:53.920 --> 00:18:54.940
How did he die?

00:18:56.900 --> 00:19:00.430
Asirpa-san, Suzukawa was a bad man.

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:03.070
Bad men don't have human hearts.

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.750
So they feel less pain than normal people.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.520
So you don't need to feel sympathy for them.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:10.790
Are you making fun of me because I'm a kid?

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.860
You can't fool me like that.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:14.890
That's what I've tried to think.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:19.640
During the war, I said that 
the enemy weren't like us.

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:21.670
They didn't suffer as they died.

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:24.900
On the battlefield,
 you need to destroy yourself

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.490
and become someone else if you want to fight.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:48.820
Otherwise, we couldn't have survived.

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:55.370
Was everyone able to go back 
to who they were before?

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:58.070
Some were, I'm sure.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:01.250
They went home, spent time 
with their families...

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:04.010
Maybe you can get the old you back that way.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:08.710
Those who couldn't go back to normal 
after coming back to Japan...

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:11.410
Their hearts are still on the battlefield.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.640
Asirpa-san, are you eating something?

00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:21.290
Deer liver.

00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:22.870
You have some, too.

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:24.990
You lost a lot of blood.

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:28.770
I want to eat the brains, too,
but we'll wait until the wind stops.

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:32.330
You really do love brains, Asirpa-san.

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:35.600
What do you love, besides osoma?

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:36.780
Food?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:39.880
Dried persimmons, I guess.

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:42.050
What's that?

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:46.470
That's right... there are no 
persimmon trees in Hokkaido.

00:20:47.570 --> 00:20:50.760
You take bitter persimmons and dry them out.

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:52.810
After you dry them, they become really sweet.

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:56.200
I haven't had one for years.

00:20:56.710 --> 00:21:00.940
The last time I did was 
before I left for the war.

00:21:02.090 --> 00:21:04.700
You didn't have any when you came back?

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.600
It was spring. There weren't any.

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.460
I see.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:19.630
If you eat dried persimmons, will you 
go back to who you were before the war?

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.810
Once it's all over...

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.900
Take me to your homeland.

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:51.450
I want to try dried persimmons, too.

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:57.000
Got it, Sugimoto?

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Ani Nekko</b>

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:39.320
Next Time: "Ani Nekko."
